sts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:49:50-08:00","id":1014026,"title":"","content":"No description of Agony Tilt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T17:34:56-08:00","id":1014063,"title":"","content":"pg 88, Supernatural Victims sidebar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but become asymptomatic<br /> vectors for the Infection for a number of days<br /> equal to <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>their</b> </span>10 minus their Supernatural Potency<br /> trait... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 12-07-2016, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T18:07:46-08:00","id":1014074,"title":"","content":"There seem to be quite a few mistakes on the firearms table on page 133. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Type</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Damage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Range<b>s</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Capacity</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Initiative</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Strength</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Size</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Availability</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Tags</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Example</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Light Pistol</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Long</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Medium</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">\u009f\u009f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">n/a</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Glock 17 (9mm)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Heavy Pistol</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">+2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Long</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Medium</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">-2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">\u009f\u009f\u009f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">n/a</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Desert Eagle</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Light Revolver</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Medium</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Medium</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>6</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>0</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">\u009f\u009f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">n/a</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">SW M29 (.38 Special)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Heavy Revolver</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">+2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Low</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Medium</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>6</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>-2</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">\u009f\u009f\u009f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">n/a</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">SW M29 (.44 Magnum)</td> </tr> </table></div> - &quot;Ranges&quot; should probably be &quot;Range&quot; or Range Band.<br /> - Both Light and Heavy Revolver have an Initiative of 6, which is presumably an artifact of the previous rules for ammo capacity. Should probably be 0 for Light Revolver and -2 for Heavy Revolver to mirror the Light and Heavy pistol.<br /> - Light revolver has a Strength requirement of 0. Should probably be 2 to mirror the Light Pistol.<br /> - Heavy Revolver has a Strength requirement of -2. Should probably be 3 to mirror the Heavy Pistol.<br /> - Heavy Revolver has a Range of Low, which is a Capacity, not a Range. Should probably be Medium to mirror Light Revolver.<br /> \u200b- Both Light and Heavy Revolver have a Capacity of Medium. This might be intentional, but since the Heavy Revolver has Low mistakenly written in its Range category, this might have been intended to be its Capacity. Either way, Light and Heavy Revolver should probably have the same Capacity. Having lower Capacity than their Pistol analogues seems more verisimilar.<br /> - Both Light and Heavy Revolver have lower range than both Light and Heavy Pistol, which seems strange to me. It's possible this is the intent, but it seems there are a lot of errors in this section of the table, so I thought I should bring it up as well, just in case the Pistols and Revolvers got their Ranges swapped (which would make more sense to me, if revolvers had longer ranges than pistols to compensate for their lower Capacity), or the Revolvers got their Ranges swapped with their Capacities (which would at least leave them both with the same Range).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-07-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:08:37-08:00","id":1014092,"title":"","content":"The melee weaponry table on page 138 has &quot;+1 Durability (katana) or +1 Initiative (long sword)&quot; as a feature of the Sword. Probably working as intended, but David has mentioned elsewhere that he may remove that in errata. Mentioning it here for the record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:09:54-08:00","id":1014112,"title":"","content":"Page 85: Not a Bug but a Feature is listed as a 2 or 3 dot merit, text refers to 3 and 5 dot effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:12:05-08:00","id":1014113,"title":"","content":"Unsure if the merit Peacemaker is meant to talk down werewolves in Basu-Im, or just Wasu-Im. This is more a question of clarity of intent, as I'm not sure if that is indeed errata, but it reads like one to me because that sounds ridiculous. Your pack can't even talk you down from death rage, unlike touchstones for Frenzy, so it jumped out to me as potentially not the intent. But I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> I know this might read as a content thing, but I'm really just saying that if it's meant to refer to Wasu-Im only it should be said, otherwise it's probably fine. Just bringing attention to the terming, I'm not worried about whether said merit is fitting with werewolf's intent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-07-2016, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:55:18-08:00","id":1014132,"title":"","content":"Page 76: Psychokinetic Combat 3, Trapped Potential, doesn't specify a size limit on the objects you can detonate. The text pretty clearly implies that it's meant for size 0-3, given that the examples are a lighter or a welding torch, the damage is limited to three bashing, and the resulting Force is Size 3, but I could see someone trying to use it on a truck, which seems beyond the scope of intent but within the rule as currently written. (Or more humorously: &quot;I blow up... THE EARTH&quot;)<br /> <br /> Also age 76: Sojourner is a neat upgrade to apportation, but while I assume it's intended to remove the drawback it doesn't say so. Thus, teleporting a person one mile would deal 1760 bashing, making it an extremely potent killing power but useless for its (presumably) intended function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T21:26:12-08:00","id":1014145,"title":"","content":"Page 76: Psychokinetic Resistance requires Psychokinesis 1, but the Psychokinesis merit is locked at either 3 or 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-08-2016, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T22:16:33-08:00","id":1014167,"title":"","content":"I don't understand what's being said in chapter 1 in regards to dramatic failures, are these any more likely? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dramatic Failure: Basic dramatic failure im-<br /> poses a Tilt selected by the Storyteller or another<br /> disadvantageous Condition. The dramatic failure<br /> only applies when a character harnesses the<br /> framing scene\u2019s advantage. In some situations the<br /> player can decide whether to suffer a dramatic<br /> failure to earn a Beat. </div> </div> </div> the way this is referred to through the chapter sounds like they're more likely to occur than they normally are, maybe I've read over it, but I don't see that either. Is this just a way to say that we should predetermine what happens if you get a dramatic failure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T23:07:47-08:00","id":1014180,"title":"","content":"Page 52: The rules for feats of strength which were in the draft of Strength Performance are absent. This makes the third maneuver &quot;Push/Pull&quot; impossible for the Storyteller to judge in play, and creates issues for the second and fourth as well.<br /> <br /> Page 135: The paragraph on explosives' Blast Area has two different descriptions of the trait - the second description starts at &quot;This trait is listed in three values ...&quot;, and is clearly wrong, since the grenade table lists only one number under Blast Area. The last two sentences of that paragraph should be cut.<br /> <br /> Please clarify if &quot;add the explosive\u2019s Damage rating in automatic successes for additional damage&quot; under Force refers to the automatic damage described under Damage, or is added to that damage. (That is, the formula is either Damage + successes on Force roll, or Damage + (successes on Force roll + Damage, if successes &gt; 0), but I don't know which.)<br /> <br /> Does &quot;Mundane armor only counts as half its ballistic rating when protecting against explosions&quot; mean that general armor doesn't reduce explosive damage at all? And does supernatural armor apply against explosive damage at its full rating by default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","user":"Michael Brazier","date":". 12-08-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T23:58:01-08:00","id":1014195,"title":"","content":"On Page 13 under What You Will Find Inside, for Chapter Four: Tokyo, cites &quot;a World of Darkness take on some of Tokyo's neighborhoods.&quot; This should probably be &quot;a Chronicles of Darkness take on some of Tokyo's neighborhoods&quot;, since the lines are supposed to be separated differently by name like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T00:00:20-08:00","id":1014196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1014195#post1014195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Page 13 under What You Will Find Inside, for Chapter Four: Tokyo, cites &amp;quot;a World of Darkness take on some of Tokyo's neighborhoods.&amp;quot; This should probably be &amp;quot;a Chronicles of Darkness take on some of Tokyo's neighborhoods&amp;quot;, since the lines are supposed to be separated differently by name like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Thanks. Thought I caught all those references. (This book was written before the words &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; were ever a thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:56:31-08:00","id":1014227,"title":"","content":"p72, Apportation should say how many yards per success, not just 'a number'.<br /> p74, Mind Control is listed as a three dot merit, but the description references 'The four dot version of this merit'<br /> p76 Psychokinetic Resistance is listed as having a Prerequisite of Psychokinesis \u2022, but the minimum value of Psychokinesis is \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> p75 Psychic Onslaught - lists prereqs as Telekinesis \u2022 or Psychokinesis \u2022, but the minimum value of Psychokinesis is \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Edit: Added more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 12-08-2016, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T07:29:41-08:00","id":1014306,"title":"","content":"p81, 1st sentence of Rio Matsumura description reads &quot;...killed in separate drink-driving incidences...&quot;, am pretty confident that should be &quot;...separate <b>drunk</b>-driving incidences...&quot;<br /> <br /> (stoopid English language...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Another one. <br /> pp 85-86 Field Handler is listed as a 1, 3, or 5 dot merit but lists 2 and 4 dot abilities in its description in addition to the 1, 3, and 5 dot ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 12-08-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T07:49:53-08:00","id":1014312,"title":"","content":"On page 135: the blast area descriptionsays: &quot;This trait is listed in three values separated by slashes. The first number is the ground zero blast area, the second number is the primary blast area, and the secondary blast area is twice this range.&quot; However, the grenade table only gives a single value under blast area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:01:47-08:00","id":1014406,"title":"","content":"Speaking of heavy weapons, this may be a bit extensive for errata, but the ranges for blast areas are in yards/meters, which is difficult to reconcile with the range band rules. However, the ranges for grenade launchers and flamethrowers are in range bands, so the heavy weapons rules aren't fully compatible with either range system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T20:03:34-08:00","id":1014584,"title":"","content":"Probably can't be fixed now, but I see Deaf as a persistent injury but not blind.<br /> <br /> Also Deaf, p58 appears to have some &quot;missing character [] boxes&quot;, which should be fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T02:28:57-08:00","id":1014660,"title":"","content":"The &quot;New Merits&quot; and &quot;New Tilts&quot; sub-bookmarks under the <b>Appendix: Equipment</b> bookmark go to the wrong pages","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T05:53:36-08:00","id":1014717,"title":"","content":"Page 119: &quot;D\u014djinshi&quot; appears with a square outline replacing its first vowel, which means the o-with-macron glyph isn't included in the PDF's font.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T09:38:45-08:00","id":1014802,"title":"","content":"Perhaps not a typo, but the Tokyo chapter features a part on doing rakugo in Gauru form.<br /> <br /> That's, er, kind of impossible. Hilarious, but impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T09:48:04-08:00","id":1014809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1014802#post1014802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps not a typo, but the Tokyo chapter features a part on doing rakugo in Gauru form.<br /> <br /> That's, er, kind of impossible. Hilarious, but impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither with form of the father, wolf gift, you can take many action not combat related?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 12-09-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:03:45-08:00","id":1014815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1014802#post1014802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps not a typo, but the Tokyo chapter features a part on doing rakugo in Gauru form.<br /> <br /> That's, er, kind of impossible. Hilarious, but impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>He must have Father's Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:09:22-08:00","id":1014818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1014815#post1014815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He must have Father's Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh.<br /> <br /> Probably should say Father's Form then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:22:13-08:00","id":1014821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1014818#post1014818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh.<br /> <br /> Probably should say Father's Form then.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a different form though, just a Gift that allows you to be in the form without raging as long as you stay out of combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:44:34-08:00","id":1014838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1014821#post1014821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really a different form though, just a Gift that allows you to be in the form without raging as long as you stay out of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amending to &quot;doing rakugo in Gauru with help of the Father's Form Gift&quot;, because as shown, I hear Gauru and think Death Rage without that qualifier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:24:49-08:00","id":1014851,"title":"","content":"A couple of notes about the Bowmanship style on page 47:<br /> - The Bullseye maneuver states, &quot;When attacking a speci- fied target you may lower your bow\u2019s damage rating to any amount (0 or greater) to add +1 and the 8-again quality to the attack roll.&quot; Is there any benefit to reducing the damage modifier by any more than 1? Seems like either the bonus dice to the attack roll should either be equal to the damage penalty, or the damage penalty should just be -1.<br /> - &quot;Your character fires her arrows and then ducks out of sight, leaving her enemies bleeding and confused. Roll Dexterity + Stealth as a reflexive action after attacking a target that is unaware of her presence. Her target must roll Wits + Composure \u2013 her successes, where failure applies the Shaken Condition to the target.&quot; The description makes it sound like the attacker would become hidden again after using the maneuver, but it isn't clear in the mechanical text if that happens or not.<br /> - Both Arcing Fire and Death from above rely on measurements in yards to work. It would be nice to add clarification on how these Maneuvers interact with the optional Range Band rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:06:52-08:00","id":1014906,"title":"","content":"Where is that werewolf mentioned anyway? I can't find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:17:50-08:00","id":1014969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1014906#post1014906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that werewolf mentioned anyway? I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I misread the post on RPGnet; it's actually in Werewolf 2nd.<br /> <br /> ...And the guy who wrote that was also wrong, because what he was remembering was Ghost Wolves using Gifts on stage, and &quot;flirting with <i>Kuruth</i>&quot;. Which is simply an example of <i>Nuzusul </i>Gonna Do What<i> Nuzusul</i> Done Do Did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 12-09-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:47:58-08:00","id":1014977,"title":"","content":"I have sent you something about the Agony Tilt via other channels, David. Not posting here because you may have some backstage decisions to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:34:30-08:00","id":1014997,"title":"","content":"I'm going to concentrate on sections I wrote. From Ch. 1 framing scenes. Yes, I am aware that this means it's my fault!<br /> <br /> <b>P. 21</b>: &quot;This book calls these spaces framing scenes. They range from entire <b>eras</b> to single, significant objects.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be: &quot;This book calls these spaces framing scenes. They range from entire areas to single, significant objects.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>End of P. 21/Beginning of P. 22: &quot;</b>The nasty dumpster we\u2019ve been using as an<b> advantage</b> is mostly this sort of scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be: &quot;The nasty dumpster we\u2019ve been using as an example is mostly this sort of scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>P. 24: &quot;</b>This grants +1 to close combat attacks, and attacks that slam characters against the floor or into padded surfaces must contend with 2 points of armor.&quot;<br /> <br /> Little awkward. Try: &quot;This grants +1 die to close combat attacks, but attacks that slam characters against the floor or padded surfaces cushion victims as if they have 2 points of armor.&quot;<br /> <br /> Under Free Fall, the &quot;human missile&quot; attack option inflicts lethal damage to both participants. That makes it sorta suicidal, when I was really thinking of the original Point Break, brah. I'd prefer it rewritten as follows:<br /> <br /> &quot;Use Dexterity + Athletics \u2013 Defense to strike as a human missile. Subtract the victim\u2019s meters or yards per turn (they're close enough that you don't need to differentiate) falling distance from the attacker\u2019s. Divide the result by 10 (rounded up) and add it as bashing damage to a successful attack, to a maximum of 10 points. The attacker suffers half of any damage inflicted, however.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>P. 25: &quot;</b>Whatever modifier you choose affects the dice pools of anyone seeking to follow, along with an additional \u20131.&quot;<br /> <br /> Better as: &quot;Whatever modifier you choose also affects the dice pools of anyone following, and adds an extra -1 as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:13:08-08:00","id":1015017,"title":"","content":"<b>P. 43: </b>The Survivalist Merit has a Style Tag. Get rid of it. The tag's nonstandard, which breaks the rules of Style Tags to begin with.<br /> <br /> <b>P. 44:</b> Second sentence on that page is scrambled and can probably just be cut.<br /> <br /> <b>P. 45:</b> I did not have access to final drafts of everything. So the following changes are necessary for Style Tags:<br /> <br /> <b>Archery: </b>Listed styles should be Bowmanship and Combat Archery.<br /> <br /> <b>Attitude:</b> Listed style should be Berserker (Enraged) and Relentless Assault (Determined). &quot;Berserk,&quot; is wrong. <br /> <br /> <b>Animal: </b>Listed styles should be K-9 (Bite) and Falconry (Claw)<br /> <br /> <b>Heavy Melee: </b>Listed styles should be Armed Defense, Heavy Weapons, Mounted Combat<br /> <br /> <b>Light Melee: </b>Listed styles should be Armed Defense, Light Weapons, Mounted Combat<br /> <br /> <b>Pistol:</b> Listed styles should be Firefight, Marksmanship, Powered Projectile<br /> <br /> <b>Pole Weapons:</b> Listed styles should be Spear and Bayonet and Staff Fighting (not just &quot;Staff&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural: </b>&quot;Adamantine&quot; Hand should be Adamant Hand, though it's now a one-off Merit and might not qualify at all. Brutal Sorcery doesn't exist and should be cut. In addition, the some of the supernatural ladder-structure powers might have a (Psychic) tag. Alternately, if you're looking for room, you might want to cut this tag completely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":".  Typo, post below notes Relentless Assault in Werewolf/Beast 12-10-2016, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T19:53:21-08:00","id":1015115,"title":"","content":"Relentless Assault appears in both Werewolf and Beast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T21:20:02-08:00","id":1015152,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 11: </b>This isn't an error, but where it gives advice on how to convert first edition weapons, it could be useful to add in a simple way of figuring out the Initiative modifier, if there <i>is </i>a one sentence way of expressing that.<br /> <b>p. 129: </b>There should be quotation marks around the chapter flavour quote, to conform with the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T06:21:43-08:00","id":1015231,"title":"","content":"pg. 143<br /> <br /> Description for the &quot;Hail of Gunfire&quot; Tilt is missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:58:53-08:00","id":1015364,"title":"","content":"Can we change Avoidance whack-a-mole<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the character gets the most successes the attack does no dam-<br /> age, and instead inflicts the Arm Wrack Tilt on the opponent. </div> </div> </div>to either allow for some damage, e.g. the opponent takes the damage they dealt instead, or at least allow it to be more stackable and based on either a GM decision or what makes sense. If I kick at you is this power useless? or how do I hurt my arm? So I can only use this once per opponent? or twice? I don't think arm wrack stacks...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:06:58-08:00","id":1016298,"title":"","content":"Hi! Long time listener, first time caller:<br /> <br /> Page 17: &quot;A lot has been written by many better-qualified people about cycles of violence, and with the word count we have, anything we could say would be reductive and problematic.&quot; The comma before the 'and' should be omitted.<br /> <br /> Page 29: &quot;See Skills in Combat (p. 59)&quot; - is missing the hyperlink on 59 and should be &quot;Violence Skills&quot; instead.<br /> <br /> Page 43: Punch Drunk - &quot;When she suffers bashing or lethal damage&quot; should be &quot;When she suffers bashing damage&quot; and a sentence needs to be added to the effect of: when all the other boxes are filled with aggravated damage then the remaining damage fills the last box as normal.<br /> Uncorrected this merit turns characters who take it into a superhero/the terminator for the price of two dots; any character who takes it can survive car bombs, being shot multiple times in the head with an antimaterial rifle, have an AK-47 filled with hollow-points shoved in their mouth and emptied, falling from the empire state building, being hit by a semi going at 200 mph, etc. They are basically unkillable as long as they have willpower to spend and only take damage from one source a turn.<br /> <br /> Page 48: Defensive Jab: A punch from the lead hand (not known for their power because of the body mechanics involved: lack of hip rotation, etc.) should not be able to damage people through full-plate or riot armor. Seriously try punching a guy wearing full plate in the face with a fast jab - you're going to hurt yourself, not him. Secondly it is unclear whether the armor piercing ability (which should be removed) applies to attacks made when Dodging.<br /> <br /> Page 61: In the 'Investigation: Watch and Learn' section. The Came Prepared Tilt is mentioned but the Tilt is not included.<br /> <br /> Page 64: &quot;Larceny comes in handy there as well, being the Skill of choice for varying your appearance.&quot; Should be Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Page 138, 154, and in other books: The Rapier entry does not describe an actual rapier but rather some sort of small sword or knife. Note that rapier's are long (3+ feet), heavy (2+ pounds) and were civilian weapons used against mostly unarmored targets (probably shouldn't have armor piercing).<br /> <br /> Page 143: 'But one (Hail of Gunfire) is an environmental Tilt.' Hail of Gunfire is not included in this section.<br /> <br /> Page 150: Resolution for the Oblivious Trait is not bolded.<br /> <br /> Page 150: Condition format is not standardized: some list Possible Sources, others do not, some omit the beats section if they don't use it while other list 'Beats: N/A'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:27:47-08:00","id":1016305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1016298#post1016298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 17: &amp;quot;A lot has been written by many better-qualified people about cycles of violence, and with the word count we have, anything we could say would be reductive and problematic.&amp;quot; The comma before the 'and' should be omitted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The coordinating conjunction &quot;and&quot; is separating two independent clauses in this sentence, so it should be preceded by a comma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:44:58-08:00","id":1016314,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 9: Appendix: Equipment</b> should be Appendix <b>One</b>: Equipment<br /> <b>p. 41:</b> <b>Go Rin no Sho </b>should be in italics.<br /> <b>p. 122: </b>&quot;She knows what she wants to do tonight, too; and whatever it is...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma (or a dash)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-12-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T01:56:59-08:00","id":1016459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1016305#post1016305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The coordinating conjunction &quot;and&quot; is separating two independent clauses in this sentence, so it should be preceded by a comma.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are of course completely correct. Something about the way the commas and parenthetical expression are used in that sentence just fries my brain when reading it, but the sentence is perfectly clear if I break it into two or use a semicolon. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:30:07-08:00","id":1016803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1016298#post1016298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 43: Punch Drunk - &quot;When she suffers bashing or lethal damage&quot; should be &quot;When she suffers bashing damage&quot; and a sentence needs to be added to the effect of: when all the other boxes are filled with aggravated damage then the remaining damage fills the last box as normal.<br /> Uncorrected this merit turns characters who take it into a superhero/the terminator for the price of two dots; any character who takes it can survive car bombs, being shot multiple times in the head with an antimaterial rifle, have an AK-47 filled with hollow-points shoved in their mouth and emptied, falling from the empire state building, being hit by a semi going at 200 mph, etc. They are basically unkillable as long as they have willpower to spend and only take damage from one source a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that was the point. To create people like Black Lagoon's Roberta, or something.<br /> <br /> Where do we go with content questions? I have found some things that are fairly silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T04:37:55-08:00","id":1016982,"title":"","content":"Punch drunk doesn't work if you're at all aggravated anyway, because you can't pay the cost of upgrading it to keep your last health box. The merit's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:13:21-08:00","id":1016990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1016982#post1016982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Punch drunk doesn't work if you're at all aggravated anyway, because you can't pay the cost of upgrading it to keep your last health box. The merit's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... Did I miss a rule that says you can't spend willpower when you have all but one box filled with aggravated damage? Because otherwise you can pay for it just fine. As a hyperbolic example of what's wrong with Punch Drunk, I present McBane's typical day:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">McBane finally has enough evidence to bring Senator Mendoza to justice. All he has to do now is testify at his trial. Unfortunately for him, Mendoza is not about to let that happen and has hired a hit-man to take McBane out before he gets there.<br /> <br /> Our scene opens in the middle of the day as the McBane gets into his car, which is parked at the top of a 10 floor parking garage. McBane puts his key in the ignition, turns it, and surprise - car bomb. The bomb is +5 damage with 6 force and McBane is at ground zero. It rolls five successes on the force dice for a total of 5 aggravated and 5 lethal. Normally this would completely incinerate McBane as he has only 8 health... except McBane has Punch Drunk so the first 5 boxes are filled with aggravated, the next two are filled with lethal, two of the remaining 3 upgrades that lethal damage to aggravated, and the remaining damage just disappears as it can't fill in the last box and can't it can't upgrade anything else. This gives a total of 7 aggravated damage. McBane staggers out of his the remains of his car, or rather, there is suddenly no car around him anymore as it has been scattered over the parking garage.<br /> <br /> The hit-man, a master sniper watching the car from a nearby rooftop through the scope of a 20mm anti-material rifle, is quite shocked to see McBane survive an explosion that would certainly have killed any normal human. Unfortunately for McBane, the hit-man has a backup plan: shooting McBane with a 20mm anti-material rifle. The hit-man rolls 5 successes on his attack and his rifle gives him +5 damage for a total of 10L. Normally this would be enough to completely blow someones brains out but since McBane has Punch Drunk, it does nothing (it can't fill in the last box because it is lethal and it can't upgrade anything else so it just goes away).<br /> <br /> The hit-man is dumbfounded - his target somehow survived being at ground zero of a car bomb followed immediately by being hit directly in the head with a 20mm round. He decides to try again and this time gets a whopping 15 successes for 20 damage. Yet even this tremendous hit gets the exact same results: McBane completely ignores something that should have blown a gaping hole through an important bit of anatomy.<br /> <br /> McBane meanwhile decides that being hit repeatedly in vital bits of his anatomy with high-powered bullets is slightly annoying so he is going get off the roof of the parking garage. But he has a dilemma as he doesn't want to walk all the way down 10 floors and the elevator is sooo slow. So he does what any rational human being would do in his situation: he jumps off the side of the parking garage. Assuming he reaches terminal velocity McBane takes 10L - and shrugs it off because of Punch Drunk.<br /> <br /> McBane then picks himself up off the asphalt (he landed in the street itself which will be important in a second) and is promptly hit by a semi (size 25) going at 60 mph. The truck rolls 10 damage on its size dice for a total of 13L damage. Which McBane ignores because he is woozy from head trauma (the meaning of being punch drunk).<br /> <br /> Picking himself up off the pavement. McBane realizes that he is going to be late for court! Hijacking the truck he rushes across town in a high-speed chase that is not relevant here.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So yeah. Punch Drunk is great if you want over the top action but it's not in keeping with the tone of the rest of the material, which is horror. As another example consider teens at a isolated camp being picked off by a slasher: the slasher is not very scary (or effective) if it takes them 6+ turns of combat to kill each teen. Also consider a hunter game: That superstrong vampire looks pretty weak if it takes them 6+ turns to kill each hunter (who meanwhile gang up and curb stomp the bastard). Or consider a military game set in the Winter War: Simo H\u00e4yh\u00e4 is perhaps the greatest sniper in history, but even he wouldn't be able to take out a target with Punch Drunk in less that 6+ turns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:30:32-08:00","id":1016997,"title":"","content":"This:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (it can't fill in the last box because it is lethal and it can't upgrade anything else so it just goes away). </div> </div> </div>is not what happens. If you can't upgrade any damage, you can't use the merit. It rolls over and you finally drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:21:31-08:00","id":1017024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1016997#post1016997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This:<br /> <br /> is not what happens. If you can't upgrade any damage, you can't use the merit. It rolls over and you finally drop.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the merit says nothing about what happens if you are unable to fully account for all the damage when upgrading. At most it vaguely implies that it cannot be used (through the word instead) when you have a completely full track. This is why I suggested stating explicitly what happens.<br /> <br /> Second, your interpretation only moves it from survive 6+ things that should kill you to 2 or 3 things that should kill you. Reiterating the McBane example a bit: suppose someone is on top of the empire state building and doesn't want to take the stairs or wait for the elevator and so jumps off. That's 10L which, for someone with 8 health, converts to 3A, 4L. They are then hit by a truck for 13L, which they will survive because they can still upgrade damage. This is why I suggested it should be bashing damage only.<br /> <br /> In short, this is I what I think the merit should do:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Effect: Your character\u2019s resolve is unwavering, even when<br /> suffering wounds, broken limbs, and lost blood. She can fight<br /> on past the point that her body demands she quit. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should allow characters to survive getting blown up with a car bomb, a direct hit from a 120 mm tank cannon, or jumping off a building instead of waiting for the elevator. Which is why I suggested the errata I did.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","user":"The Demon Code","date":".  Fixed Grammer 12-14-2016, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T07:12:14-08:00","id":1017046,"title":"","content":"Getting hit by a truck would be aggravated for a mortal.<br /> <br /> Look, the fact that you had the guy shrug off 10L to the face says to me that the problem here isn't the merit. That interpretation is <i>clearly </i>bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 12-14-2016, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:16:50-08:00","id":1017131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1016990#post1016990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... Did I miss a rule that says you can't spend willpower when you have all but one box filled with aggravated damage? Because otherwise you can pay for it just fine. </div> </div> </div> </div>You will most likely be unconscious, and therefore unable to spend Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:53:57-08:00","id":1017153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017131#post1017131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You will most likely be unconscious, and therefore unable to spend Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... as far as I can tell, as long as your rightmost health box doesn't have any damage in it you won't be unconscious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:08:18-08:00","id":1017159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017153#post1017153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... as far as I can tell, as long as your rightmost health box doesn't have any damage in it you won't be unconscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>'When a character's rightmost Health box has bashing damage marked in it, his player must make a reflexive Stamina roll each turn for him to remain conscious.'<br /> <br /> 'When a character's rightmost Health box has lethal damage marked in it, he takes another point of damage each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) until he receives medical attention, mundane or supernatural.'<br /> <br /> Potentially you could avoid losing consciousness. Having your rightmost box full of Lethal doesn't allow you to ignore the Bashing drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:19:11-08:00","id":1017166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017159#post1017159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'When a character's rightmost Health box has bashing damage marked in it, his player must make a reflexive Stamina roll each turn for him to remain conscious.'<br /> <br /> 'When a character's rightmost Health box has lethal damage marked in it, he takes another point of damage each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) until he receives medical attention, mundane or supernatural.'<br /> <br /> Potentially you could avoid losing consciousness. Having your rightmost box full of Lethal doesn't allow you to ignore the Bashing drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the information I found. So as long as you are using Punch Drunk, you won't lose consciousness as it prevents damage in your rightmost health box.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as I can tell vehicles do not do aggravated damage to mortals: they do lethal damage equal to successes rolled on size + a damage modifier based on speed (+1/20 mph).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:23:14-08:00","id":1017169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017024#post1017024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the merit says nothing about what happens if you are unable to fully account for all the damage when upgrading. At most it vaguely implies that it cannot be used (through the word instead) when you have a completely full track. This is why I suggested stating explicitly what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, here's something you need to understand about Chronicles of Darkness. The books are written in natural language, not technical language, so if &quot;the book implies XYZ but doesn't explicitly state it&quot; is going to cause problems for you, you are going to run into a lot of problems with this game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017024#post1017024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, your interpretation only moves it from survive 6+ things that should kill you to 2 or 3 things that should kill you. Reiterating the McBane example a bit: suppose someone is on top of the empire state building and doesn't want to take the stairs or wait for the elevator and so jumps off. That's 10L which, for someone with 8 health, converts to 3A, 4L. They are then hit by a truck for 13L, which they will survive because they can still upgrade damage. This is why I suggested it should be bashing damage only.</div> </div> </div> </div>These things should really be doing aggravated damage. Anything that completely destroys large quantities of tissue gets upgraded to agg for humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017024#post1017024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, this is I what I think the merit should do:<br /> <br /> I don't think it should allow characters to survive getting blown up with a car bomb, a direct hit from a 120 mm tank cannon, or jumping off a building instead of waiting for the elevator. Which is why I suggested the errata I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems your overly technical interpretation of the rules is leading to them not working as intended. I would recommend revising your interpretation. It's clear that the intent is that when it is no longer possible to upgrade wounds in your other health boxes, that the rightmost box should take the damage. It's also clear that if a source of damage would turn someone into chunky salsa, such as being at ground zero of an explosion, or being hit by a tank cannon, they should take aggravated damage. These things don't really need to be written technically perfectly, because every game is run by a human being who can interpret the natural language and apply common sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:29:15-08:00","id":1017177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017166#post1017166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly the information I found. So as long as you are using Punch Drunk, you won't lose consciousness as it prevents damage in your rightmost health box.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct about this, this appears to be the main purpose of Punch Drunk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017166#post1017166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as far as I can tell vehicles do not do aggravated damage to mortals: they do lethal damage equal to successes rolled on size + a damage modifier based on speed (+1/20 mph).</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically, yes, but damage that completely destroys large quantities of tissue get upgraded to agg against mortals. If you're getting hit by an out of control Camrey at 40 mph, yeah, you take like 10 lethal. If you get hit by an 18 wheeler at 70 mph, it's safe to say you're taking agg. And honestly, at that point you can probably ignore the damage track all together and just say the character is killed, because we are all rational beings that don't need RPG rules to tell us that if you get hit by a speeding semi, you will die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-14-2016, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:56:49-08:00","id":1017234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017177#post1017177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems your overly technical interpretation of the rules is leading to them not working as intended. I would recommend revising your interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you know, you could just apply a minor errata and fix the merit, like I recommended? Which is sort of the point of this thread. Let's be honest: falling rules work perfectly fine without Punch Drunk, damage from weapons works perfectly fine without Punch Drunk, the vehicle collision rules work fine without Punch Drunk, the explosion rules work adequatly without Punch Drunk, etc. The problem isn't with the rest of the rules or my RAW interpretation of them, it's with Punch Drunk. Which is why I recommend changing Punch Drunk not the rest of the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's clear that the intent is that when it is no longer possible to upgrade wounds in your other health boxes, that the rightmost box should take the damage. </div> </div> </div>If that is the intent, why not just change the wording slightly, <b>which I recommended in my original post</b>, to make this explicit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also clear that if a source of damage would turn someone into chunky salsa, such as being at ground zero of an explosion, or being hit by a tank cannon, they should take aggravated damage. These things don't really need to be written technically perfectly, because every game is run by a human being who can interpret the natural language and apply common sense. </div> </div> </div>Except my whole problem with Punch Drunk (and with the second dot of boxing for that matter) is that it <b>DEFIES</b> common sense. This is what the examples above are trying to show through the use of hyperbole. What it does (prevents you from filling the last box of health if you spend a willpower) allows you to do absurd things because of the way it is written and I am trying to point this out. You answer to me complaining that &quot;this defies common sense&quot; is to say &quot;apply common sense&quot;? Well that's great and all, but why not fix the &quot;defies common sense&quot; part now, while you have the opportunity?<br /> <br /> Finally, this is an errata thread. A bit of time could be used to clean up the merit so that it does what it says in the preamble explicitly in order to prevent future consternation when a player reads the rule one way and the GM another. I am not asking for a twenty page legal document explaining how the merit works. I am suggesting two minor changes: make it work for bashing only and/or make it clear that if everything else is aggravated the merit does not protect the last box.<br /> <br /> Here:<br /> <br /> &quot;Effect: Your character\u2019s resolve is unwavering, even when suffering wounds, broken limbs, and lost blood. She can fight on past the point that her body demands she quit. When she suffers bashing damage that would remove her last Health box, you may spend a point of Willpower to keep the last box, and instead upgrade damage in her other Health boxes first. If it is no longer possible to upgrade wounds in your other health boxes, any excess damage should be applied to the rightmost health box as normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Typically, yes, but damage that completely destroys large quantities of tissue get upgraded to agg against mortals. If you're getting hit by an out of control Camrey at 40 mph, yeah, you take like 10 lethal. If you get hit by an 18 wheeler at 70 mph, it's safe to say you're taking agg. </div> </div> </div>Well yes. But that is because normally the damage fills all boxes and wraps around to aggro. Getting hit by a 18 wheeler (size 25 or so) at 70 MPH (+4 Damage) will kill most people because it will do 12L damage on average (and possibly much more) which for someone with 7 health will fill most of their track with aggro instantly. The vehicle collision rules work fine (or well enough for me). The problem is when they are combined with something that defies common sense like the (as currently written) Punch Drunk merit, in which case things start to get wonky.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:14:19-08:00","id":1017255,"title":"","content":"I think with punch drunk if something would ultimately deal aggravated due to wrap around then it would count as aggravated damage overall. Which would negate punch drunk. You could read it as only damage that was originally listed as aggravated but that sounds a little extreme and supernatural rather than resilient.<br /> <br /> Could certainly use a bit of clarification though because there are several cases things don't seem so clear. If the damage would do even a single point of aggravated damage do you simply ignore the effects of the merit or do u let the merit work as intended as u fill the health boxes until you mark the first aggravated and then shift down that lethal.<br /> <br /> For simplicity sake. Id go with it simply saying if a attack would result in even a single point of aggravated damage before factoring this merit then this merit is ignored entirely. That puts it in the proper perspective.<br /> <br /> Sure, u can stay up for many punches to the head but as soon as one of those punches would wrap to aggravated you simply ignore the merit. Even the idea of someone with 2 stamina having 6 aggravated with their last box unmarked seems really wrong to me. I'll likely be ruling it as detailed above for my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 12-14-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:39:28-08:00","id":1017280,"title":"","content":"Your entire problem is based on the assumption that damage in excess of the remaining boxes simply vanishes when you use the merit, because the text doesn't explicitly say otherwise. If you read it with an eye towards reasonable intent instead of arbitrary technicality it's pretty obvious that damage in excess of your remaining boxes doesn't disappear, it rolls over into your last box and kills you. Yeah, they could add a sentence to clarify this, but that's approaching the level of &quot;We need a rule for how you stop drowning, because currently you just keep taking damage until you die&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:53:34-08:00","id":1017296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demon Code</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1017234#post1017234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes. But that is because normally the damage fills all boxes and wraps around to aggro.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's actually being upgraded. Werewolves have an actual <i>power</i> that makes them work like this instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T09:24:12-08:00","id":1017682,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 79; </b>Unsure if this was intentional or not, but the Damn Lucky merit for the Atariya template goes from <i>one dot to four dots</i>. The other &quot;starter&quot; merits for the other templates (aside from Plain Reader) go from <i>one dot to five dots</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:53:11-08:00","id":1018053,"title":"","content":"p. 107+ - The Tokyo section jumps between using 'We' and 'I'.<br /> p. 116 - Wong Ng has defense 6 but I think it should be 5 (2 Wits + 3 Athletics).<br /> p. 117 - Not sure on this one but as a (former?) ghost, shouldn't Tek-Tek have a virtue and vice? Also as a spirit of death, shouldn't she have 'Death' or similar influence?<br /> p. 119 - There is an extra newline after the yellow submarine section.<br /> p. 119 - &quot;D\u014djinshi&quot; seems to be written as &quot;D jinshi&quot;<br /> p. 120 - Tek-Tek is spelled Teke Teke on p. 120 but Tek-Tek earlier.<br /> p. 120 - Paragraph break after 'however' seems weird.<br /> p. 122 - Stephanie is missing everything after merits in her stat block.<br /> p. 122 - Mark is missing his virtue and vice.<br /> p. 125 - &quot;His Japanese his spoken&quot; should be &quot;is spoken&quot;.<br /> p. 126 - &quot;Built to Western specifications it is built upon the site of the old northeastern entrance into Edo and its lands make up much of what was once the larger Kan\u2019ei-ji temple.&quot; Needs commas and maybe restructuring to remove one of the 'built'.<br /> p. 127 - Skills and merits are messed up: martial arts is in the skill section, brawl is missing, and &quot;Fighting Style: 3&quot; should specify the style.<br /> p. 128 - Defense should be 4 (Wits 3 + Athletics 1). Health should be 6 (Size 5 + Stamina 1). Integrity score is included in the merits. Fighting Style is missing which style it is.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T12:29:05-08:00","id":1018865,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 45:</b> &quot;Default Keywords:<b> Agile Strong</b>...&quot; -- should be a comma between those<br /> <b>p. 45: </b>&quot;The character needs to first possess as many Merit dots <b>in same</b> Style Tag as the rank...&quot; -- missing a <b>the</b><br /> <b>p. 54:</b> &quot;<b>Thus </b>maneuver inflicts one point of bashing damage...&quot; -- should be <b>this</b><br /> <b>p. 56: </b>The sidebar is supposed to be part of the next section, but it's placed a bit awkwardly<br /> <b>p. 56: </b>&quot;That means any injury system must follow this<b> ethos; </b>and...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma (or cut the <i>and</i>)<br /> <b>p. 139: </b>The term definitions at the bottom of the page don't quite match up with the chart. It doesn't define <b>Effect</b>; it defines <b>Examples</b>, but only the Ranged Weapon chart uses that category. Also, <b>Initiative:</b> isn't in bold.<br /> <b>p. 152: </b>All the stuff Charlaquin mentioned about <b>p. 133</b>.<br /> <b>p. 154: </b>&quot;See staking rules (p. <b>XX</b>)&quot; -- Page XX rears its ugly head; it's not replicated on the chart on 138, but maybe the <b>CofD </b>page reference for the special rules should be included, if they're not somewhere in <b>Hurt Locker</b>.<br /> <b>p. 154: </b>Same thing Charlaquin said about katanas and what not<br /> <b>p. 155: </b>Same errors as listed above on <b>p. 139</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-18-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T22:31:22-08:00","id":1019620,"title":"","content":"It's pretty self-evident that the next damage &quot;upgrade&quot; past aggravated is He's Dead, Jim. In 1e this was actually codified in Mummy but that was not moved to core rules, it being assumed that people who are not imperishable corpses animated by Fate had no use for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:24:55-08:00","id":1019836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013912-hurt-locker-errata-thread?p=1019620#post1019620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty self-evident that the next damage &quot;upgrade&quot; past aggravated is He's Dead, Jim. In 1e this was actually codified in Mummy but that was not moved to core rules, it being assumed that people who are not imperishable corpses animated by Fate had no use for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that represented by a completely filled in Health Box, then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}